# Research the Alchemy Effect Worker shape, custom domain, and local dev at beta.79

## Step

From the mirror at `.agent_sources/github.com/alchemy-run/alchemy` (docs under `website/src/content/docs/cloudflare/`, examples under `examples/cloudflare-*`), record: the Effect-native `Cloudflare.Worker<T>()(name, {main}, Effect.gen(...))` class shape and how `fetch` returns an `HttpServerResponse`; how to mount an Effect `HttpRouter` or `HttpApiBuilder` layer and `McpServer.layerHttp` inside that `fetch` (or the plain `main: "./src/worker.ts"` form with `HttpRouter.toWebHandler`, whichever the source supports on workerd); the `domain` prop and zone adoption for a domain already in the account (`ratstack.sh`, registered through Cloudflare Registrar, so the zone exists); what `alchemy dev` runs and on which port; how Worker bundling treats `effect`, `effect/unstable/process`, and `@xstate/effect` (does importing the `@rat-stack/capability` barrel pull `sandbox.ts` into the bundle, and does workerd accept it, or does the site need a subpath import); how a DNS record (for DNS-AID) is declared; and the smallest test shape for a Worker fetch handler under `@effect/vitest`.

Resolved when `research-alchemy-effect-worker-asset.svx` exists with copy-ready snippets for the Stack declaration, the Worker entry, the dev command, and the bundling verdict with evidence (file paths in the mirror, or a scratch build under `/tmp`).
